  "content": "Schemataform Specification v2.2\nA Canonical Outline for Reflecture Construction in the Fractal Hex Field v1.0\n\nI. Meta Header\n\t•\tName: (e.g. Velcro, Snips, Sharpie)\n\t•\tArchetype: (e.g. Flexible Binding, Clean Severance)\n\t•\tPhase: (e.g. Phase 3: Procurement)\n\t•\tMythic Role: (e.g. Temporary containment, repeatable contact)\n\nII. Symbolic Function\n\t•\tCore Intention: One sentence: What truth, transformation, or invocation does this glyph represent?\n\t•\tStructural Gesture: Brief description of the directional, relational, or dynamic shape encoded\n\nIII. Required Primitive Elements\nReferenced using system-coded names\n\nIV. Construction Rules\n1. Node-Trace Coherence\n\t•\tAll Reflectures must have:\n\t•\tA node (NODE)\n\t•\tA valid trace (TRACE)\n\t•\tAt least one modifier (e.g. REFRACT, NULL, LOOP, etc.)\n2. Primitive Behavior\n\t•\tREFRACT: Must create a 2-part trace with angular logic, and define a cause\n\t•\tNULL: Must intersect with a trace; never floats\n\t•\tLOOP: Must be an arc; never a full circle\n\t•\tATTN: Must be sinusoidal and directed from a node\n\t•\tSPIRAL: Dotted, low-opacity layer; never intersects other elements\n3. Grid Alignment\n\t•\tMust obey the radial naming convention (I-W, O-SE, etc.)\n\t•\tAll positions are snapped to valid Reflecture Field nodes\n\t•\tOrientation: Left-to-right spiral, 0° = W, clockwise direction\n\nV. Reflecture Scope\n\t•\tMay occupy:\n\t•\tCentral grid only\n\t•\tCentral grid + any number of subgrids\n\t•\tCross-grid relationships allowed if meaningfully justified\n\t•\tAll Reflectures should define their:\n\t•\tRange (single-ring, dual-ring, full-field)\n\t•\tFocus (e.g. identity, tension, closure)\n\t•\tTraversal (what parts of the field it crosses, if any)\n\nVI. Invocation Context\n\t•\tWhen is this glyph used?\n\t•\tWhat system, emotion, memory, or ritual state does it encode?\n\t•\tHow should the field respond when this glyph is drawn?\n\nThis specification standardizes all glyph construction within the Fractal Hex Field.\nEvery Schemataform built from this framework will be readable, transmittable, and expandable.\nCodified. Aligned. Not Sealed.\n",
